      "id": "experimentguard",
      "summary": "Own finite minimum experiment sets, observation-driven iteration, optional holdout checks and bounded terminal decisions.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Distinguish hypotheses only within the caller-declared finite experiment-count limit and report limit failures separately from truly indistinguishable pairs.",
        "License native closure only for a unique consistent hypothesis with no holdout counterexample and no gaps, while preserving the finite iteration limit first; holdout observations are optional.",
        "Continue a bounded multi-survivor iteration only with a concrete distinguishing next candidate; do not infer historical evidence progress from unchanged gap identifiers; malformed specs return one JSON error."
